<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles III, Duke of Bourbon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1490">1490</a>–<a href="/years/1527">1527</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Constable of Bourbon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles III, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a>, was Constable of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the greatest noble of the kingdom. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a> and his mother challenged his inheritance, he went over to Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> in 1523, and his lands were confiscated. He commanded imperial troops at Pavia and was killed leading the attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 1527, which became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sack-of-rome-1527">Sack of Rome</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-iii-duke-of-bourbon.jpg" alt="Charles III, Duke of Bourbon" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Clouet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Connetable_Bourbon.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
